  "title": "A position sent at the receipt's own instant is in the 7-day look-back",
  "rules": ["lnk_01", "lnk_02", "lnk_04", "lnk_05"],
  "reasoning": [
    "Casey's Q2 answer (PR #66 comment 6968763406, item 2), as PR #67 words it in lnk_02: \"a position at the receipt's own instant is inside the 7 days before it\".",
    "c46-r sent cell C (20 bits) at 22 09:05 and cell D (20 bits, box d20, about 1 km north of C) at 23 10:10:00, the instant of its first receipt. C and D neither overlap nor lie within 40 m of each other. Every receipt is a direct hop (lnk_01).",
    "Receipt at 10:10:00: its look-back holds C and D, which are not the same place, so c46-r has moved and takes the position nearest in time within 30 minutes, D at 0 minutes. Receipts at 10:20 and 10:30: the look-back again holds C and D, and D (10 and 20 minutes before) is the only position within 30 minutes. Every receipt uses d20 (lnk_02, step 5).",
    "If the receipt's own instant were left out of the look-back, the 10:10 receipt would see only C, be stationary on C's cell, and the hour would hold two relayer boxes and be dropped by step 8.",
    "c46-r is not stationary at every receipt, so each receipt keeps its own box (step 6); all three use d20, so the hour has one box (step 8). Each receipt passes lnk_05 at 3021.476 m from d20 to g16. 3 packets: kept. Medians: SNR 5, 6 and 7 dB give 6.0; RSSI -90, -95 and -100 dBm give -95.0. position_uncertainty_m is d20 22.734445 m plus g16 363.750397 m, = 386.484842 m. Neither end is precise: both were sent on the public broker only."
  ],
